# Playwright review screenshots. These are WRITTEN by the suite and never compared
# against, so committing them just churns binary diffs on every run — and a run
# that catches a page mid-load bakes a useless "baseline" into history.
tests/visual/__shots__/

# 2026-08-01 content-rewrite + Codex working files.
#
# `research/rw/` is the rewrite fleet's input and output: 35 per-lesson input
# extracts and 42 patch files, all already merged into src/content/data via
# merge-code.cjs and patch-why.cjs. `research/codex/` is the same for the Codex —
# 31 authored micro-batches plus two repair lists, all merged into codex.json.
# Both are reproducible from the shipped data and the contracts, and together they
# are 3.6MB of intermediate JSON that would churn on every future pass.
#
# The CONTRACTS are the artifacts worth keeping, and they live in docs/curriculum/
# (tracked), not here. The SD art spec is un-ignored below: it is the input the
# owner needs on the machine that actually has Stable Diffusion.
research/rw/
research/codex/
research/rewrite/
research/walk/
!research/codex-art-specs.json

# One-off diagnostic drivers, hardcoded to a single lesson and superseded by
# tests/visual/. Screenshots they wrote are in research/walk/, already ignored.
tools/diag-*.mjs
tools/walk.mjs

# 2026-08-02 transformation working files: the 26 cloud-platform concept extracts
# fed to the check-authoring fleet and its raw output batches. Both are merged
# into src/content/data/checks.json via tools/merge-checks.cjs, and both are
# reproducible from the shipped spine — the artifact worth keeping is the
# validating merge script and its self-test, which are tracked in tools/.
research/cp-concepts.json
research/cp-batches/
research/cp-out/

